**Minor towel-related spoilers ahead**

According to the hitch Hiker's Guide, a towel is the most useful thing
a person can possibly own. After reading the recently-posted
beginner's guide to 3.4.1, I'm lead to understand that this is the
reason they are included in nethack.

Except they aren't very useful.

AFAIK (having consulted a few spoilers) they are only good for
blindfolding yourself (which you can do with a blindfold), for #wiping
pie off your face (which you can do without a towel) and for cleaning
up greasy fingers (not that common a problem.)

If there are other uses for a towel, what are they? I'd love to know.
If not, what other ones could be added to the game? Here are a few
ideas:

* (w)ielding a towel allows you to twist it up and flick monsters with
it as a weapon, or maybe you could use it as a sling.
* (w)ielding a towel against a water elemental or other liquid
adversary could absorb the monster bit by bit- equivalent to a level
drain attack.
* (t)hrowing or (d)ropping a towel into a puddle/ rust trap soaks up
all the water and allows you to cross safely.
* #rubbing a towel on a metallic item immediately after that item got
splashed with water or acid might prevent rusting/ corrosion.
* You could (W)ear a towel on your head. It wouldn't offer much
protection without some scrolls of enchant armour though.
* (a)pplying a towel to a foocatrice corpse would allow you to wrap it
up and carry it safely(ish) without gloves (although you shouldn't be
able to wield the corpse like this).
* (a)pplying a towel to an egg wraps it up warm and encourages it to
hatch.
* (a)pply a towel to a pet and you can use it as a lead/ leash. 
* #dipping a towel into holy water and then laying it on the floor
creates a barrier that undead and other unholy creatures cannot cross.
* #dipping a towel into a potion of (extra|full) healing and then
(W)earing it on your head gives you a limited regeneration ability.
* #dipping a towel into a potion of levitation turns it (temporarily)
into a flying carpet.
* #dipping a towel into a potion of invisibility turns the towel into
a cloak or invisibility.
* writing on a towel with a magic marker turns the towel into a cloak
of magic absorption (aka magic resistance).

And so on. Of course some of the above might be pointless and/or
unbalancing and/or not worth the required programming time, but it
seems to me towels are an under-used resource. Make towels universal
enough and it could even lead to a new conduct: Towel-only, where the
only thing you're allowed to wield, wear or apply for the entire game
is a towel.

